# Kafka Clone

A small Kafka-inspired message broker built from scratch in Python.

The goal of this project is not to reproduce Apache Kafka completely, but to understand the core concepts behind a distributed messaging system by implementing them incrementally.

## Current Architecture

```text
Producer
   │
   │ TCP
   ▼
Broker
   │
   ▼
Topic
   │
   ├── Partition 0
   │      └── Log
   │
   ├── Partition 1
   │      └── Log
   │
   └── Partition 2
          └── Log
```

## Current Features

* Persistent append-only log
* Logical message offsets
* Offset → disk-position index
* TCP broker
* TCP request/response framing
* Persistent producer connection
* Persistent consumer connection
* Consumer offset persistence
* Consumer polling for new messages
* Multiple concurrent TCP clients using threads
* Partition abstraction
* Partition persistence
* Automated tests with pytest

